
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
############################  0 - OVERVIEW  #######################################
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This repo builds the country-level damage-function input for "Valuing global wildfire
PM2.5 mortality caused by climate change" (Williams, Fremstad, Burkhardt, Lou;
Fire_SC_CO2_draft.pdf). The paper estimates a fifth GIVE damage sector -- wildfire
PM2.5 mortality -- and needs, for each country c, beta_c: the change in
population-weighted per-capita fire PM2.5 exposure (ug/m3/yr) per 1C increase in
global mean temperature (GMT).

This R pipeline produces beta_c (and a grid-cell analog, beta_i, used only to map the
spatial pattern). It:

  1) extracts gridded fire PM2.5 and population data from three source studies
     (Pierce et al. 2017 / CESM, Park et al. 2024 / CLASSIC-JULES-SSiB4, Zhao et al. 2025),
  2) regrids everything onto a common 0.5deg population grid and assigns country codes,
  3) pairs each grid cell/country observation with its GMT anomaly, and
  4) runs country- and grid-cell-level fixed-effects regressions of fire PM2.5 on GMT.

The resulting beta_c estimates (output/betas/fpm_gmt_betas_country_full.csv)
are the damage-function parameter that feeds the GIVE/SC-CO2 valuation step,
which lives outside this repo (see note at the top of Section 5 below).

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
############################  1 - DIRECTORY STRUCTURE  #######################################
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

fire-pm25-temperature-response/
|-- README
|-- Fire_SC_CO2_draft.pdf        manuscript draft
|-- code/
|   |-- pierce_etal_2017/        extract + regrid Pierce/CESM PM2.5 and population
|   |-- park_etal_2024/          extract + regrid Park historical PM2.5 and population
|   |-- zhao_etal_2025/          regrid Zhao projected PM2.5 and population
|   |-- other_mapping/           country-code assignment, death-rate join
|   |-- gmt_chg/                 GMT anomaly series for all three studies
|   |-- regression_beta/         beta_c / beta_i regressions, GIVE country mapping, tables
|   |   |-- regression/            main spec + leave-one-model-out sensitivity (country & grid)
|   |-- plots/                   figures built from regression outputs
|-- input/                       raw source data (NetCDF/CSV/.mat/.npz) -- see Section 4
|   |-- pierce_etal_2017/
|   |-- Park_etal_2024/
|   |-- Zhao_etal_2025/
|   |-- GIVE/
|   |-- WB_crude_death_rate/
|   |-- landmask_area/
|   |-- temperature/
|-- output/                      processed CSVs, regression coefficients, latex tables
|   |-- pm_joined/
|   |-- gmt/
|   |-- betas/
|   |-- GIVE_betas/
|   |-- latex/
|-- images/                      manuscript figures + diagnostic maps
    |-- regression_beta/
    |-- pm/
    |-- fpm_cell_global/
    |-- fpm_cell_usa/

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
############################  2 - FILE EXECUTION ORDER  #######################################
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Run stages top-to-bottom, and run the files listed within each stage top-to-bottom too.
Three source studies are extracted/regridded in parallel as lettered sub-groups (a)/(b)/(c)
within Stage 1 -- run those in listed order; "<- needs ..." notes call out dependencies.

STAGE 1 -- per-study extraction & regridding (parallel)

  (a) Pierce et al. 2017 (CESM):
      code/pierce_etal_2017/NetCDF_extract_pm.R
      code/pierce_etal_2017/NetCDF_extract_pop_final.R
      code/pierce_etal_2017/pm_to_pop_regrid.R          <- needs both files above

  (b) Park et al. 2024:
      code/park_etal_2024/pop_regrid_park_2024.R
      code/park_etal_2024/pm_regrid_park_2024.R          <- needs pm_to_pop_regrid.R output

  (c) Zhao et al. 2025:
      code/zhao_etal_2025/pop_regrid_zhao_2025.R
      code/zhao_etal_2025/pm_regrid_zhao_2025.R          <- needs pm_regrid_park_2024.R
                                                              and pop_regrid_zhao_2025.R output

  (d) GMT (independent of a-c):
      code/gmt_chg/temp_chg.R

STAGE 2 -- merge & country mapping (needs 1c)

  code/other_mapping/country_map_pop_pm_final.R
  code/other_mapping/death_rate_processing.R             <- needs country_map_pop_pm_final.R

STAGE 3 -- country-level aggregation (needs 2)

  code/regression_beta/pop_wght_pm_cntry.R

STAGE 4 -- regressions (needs Stage 3 and/or Stage 2 grid data, plus Stage 1d GMT)

  code/regression_beta/regression/fpm_gmt_regress_country.R   (country-level; fits the main
                                                    spec AND 5 leave-one-model-out sensitivity
                                                    variants in one loop -> beta_c per group)
  code/regression_beta/regression/fpm_gmt_regress_grid.R      (same main + leave-one-model-out
                                                    design at the grid-cell level -> beta_i)
  code/regression_beta/regress_desc_stats.R        (descriptive stats + Figure 4; reads the
                                                    "full" group output written above)

STAGE 5 -- comparison, GIVE mapping, and plots (needs Stage 4 outputs)

  code/regression_beta/beta_comparison_latex.R     -> Tables 4-5 (main vs. each excl_* group)
  code/regression_beta/beta_GIVE_country_map.R     -> maps beta_c (main + each excl_* group)
                                                       onto the full GIVE country list
  code/plots/plots_beta_lobf.R                     -> Figures 3, 5 (main/"full" group)
  code/plots/plots_beta_lobf_grid.R                -> Figures 1, 6, for all 6 groups
  code/plots/plots_stats_fpm_all.R                 -> descriptive plots across all datasets

DIAGNOSTIC / VALIDATION UTILITIES (not part of the main pipeline; run standalone for QC)

  code/other_mapping/country_map_pop_pm_validation.R   -- pierce data (CLM file) vs. World Bank population check
  code/park_etal_2024/org_park_summary.R                -- yearly PM2.5 summary stats by model
  code/park_etal_2024/sanity_check_pm_park_us_all.R     -- CONUS PM2.5 map QC
  code/park_etal_2024/sanity_check_pm_park_world_classic.R -- global PM2.5 map QC (CLASSIC)
  code/park_etal_2024/sanity_check_pop_park_2024.R      -- city-level population QC
  code/park_etal_2024/coordinate_check_park.R           -- inspect a single Park NetCDF's
                                                            native grid (centers vs. edges)
  code/pierce_etal_2017/pm_pop_edge_center_check.R      -- confirm whether Pierce PM2.5/pop
                                                            NetCDF coords are centers or edges

  IMPORTANT: what happens after beta_c leaves this repo (Monte Carlo sampling of beta_c and
  the concentration-response coefficient, the GIVE wildfire-PM2.5 damage function, discounting,
  and the resulting SC-CO2) is not implemented in this repo -- see the flagged items in
  Section 5 below.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
############################  3 - CODE SUMMARY  #######################################
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

pierce_etal_2017/
  NetCDF_extract_pm.R          Extract fire PM2.5 (fPM = total - no-fire) at the grid-cell
                                level from Pierce CESM NetCDFs; monthly + annual-average,
                                for 2000/2050/2100 x RCP4.5/8.5, with/without human influence.
  NetCDF_extract_pop_final.R   Build per-cell population (2001-2010) from the CLM SSP1 NetCDF,
                                converting density to totals via grid-cell area.
  pm_to_pop_regrid.R           Re-grid coarse (1.25deg) PM2.5 onto the fine (0.5deg) population
                                grid by nearest-neighbor matching; merge into one table.
  pm_pop_edge_center_check.R   Diagnostic: confirm whether PM2.5 and population NetCDF
                                coordinates are cell centers or edges, before regridding.

park_etal_2024/
  pop_regrid_park_2024.R       Convert the Park .mat population grid (360x720x6 decades) to a
                                tidy CSV, area-weighted (sum) regridded onto the 0.5deg grid.
  pm_regrid_park_2024.R        Process GEOS-Chem PM2.5 output (CLASSIC/JULES/SSiB4 vs.
                                withoutfire) into fPM by model x decade; merge into the
                                master pop_pm table; validate against authors' results1206.mat.
  org_park_summary.R           Diagnostic: yearly min/max/mean/median PM2.5 by land-surface
                                model, straight from the raw NetCDFs.
  sanity_check_pm_park_*.R     Diagnostic: render CONUS / global PM2.5 choropleth maps as
                                self-contained HTML for visual QC of the regridded PM2.5.
  sanity_check_pop_park_2024.R Diagnostic: spot-check regridded population for 5 US cities.
  coordinate_check_park.R      Diagnostic: read one Park NetCDF and confirm whether its
                                native grid coordinates are cell centers or edges.

zhao_etal_2025/
  pop_regrid_zhao_2025.R       Convert the Zhao 0.1deg population .npz to a 0.5deg long-format
                                CSV via area-weighted (sum) resampling, conserving total pop.
  pm_regrid_zhao_2025.R        Area-weight-average Zhao 0.1deg PM2.5 (4 scenario CSVs: SSP245/
                                585 x with/without fire) to 0.5deg; compute fPM; merge into the
                                master pop_pm table -> pop_pm_combined_final.csv.

gmt_chg/
  temp_chg.R                   Compute GMT anomaly (degC, relative to 1850-1900) for every
                                period/decade/scenario used downstream, from three sources:
                                Pierce CESM NetCDFs (area-weighted), OWID observed series
                                (Park decades), and MimiSSP series (Zhao SSPs).

other_mapping/
  country_map_pop_pm_final.R   Assign each 0.5deg grid cell to a country by max-overlap-area
                                intersection with Natural Earth polygons; filter to GIVE
                                countries; QC against Park population.
  country_map_pop_pm_validation.R  Diagnostic: validate CLM-derived country population totals
                                against World Bank official totals.
  death_rate_processing.R      Join World Bank crude death rates (1960-2020) onto the grid,
                                filling unmatched cells with the world average.

regression_beta/
  pop_wght_pm_cntry.R           Aggregate grid-cell fPM to country-level population-weighted
                                per-capita exposure (all three studies); append death rates
                                and a global row.
  regression/fpm_gmt_regress_country.R  MAIN + SENSITIVITY, in one script: country-level FE
                                regression of fPM on GMT, pooled across Pierce/Park/Zhao with
                                fire-model fixed effects (Park factual + counterfactual runs of
                                the same model pooled into one FE level). Fits the full 5-FE-
                                level model (-> beta_c, Equation 1 in the paper) plus 5 leave-
                                one-model-out variants (excl_CESM/classic/jules/ssib4/Zhao) that
                                each drop one fire-model source entirely, to test whether
                                beta_c depends on any single data source.
  regression/fpm_gmt_regress_grid.R     Same main + leave-one-model-out design at the grid-cell
                                level -> beta_i per group, used to characterize the spatial
                                pattern and its sensitivity to any one source (Figures 1, 6).
  regress_desc_stats.R         Descriptive statistics for the regression inputs and the
                                main ("full" group) estimates; produces Figure 4.
  beta_comparison_latex.R      Compare beta_c across the main spec and the 5 leave-one-model-
                                out variants; exports Tables 4-5 as LaTeX.
  beta_GIVE_country_map.R      Left-join beta_c estimates (main + each leave-one-model-out
                                variant) onto the full GIVE country list.

plots/
  plots_beta_lobf.R            Country-level beta_c (main/"full" group): histogram +
                                choropleth combined multiplot, standalone map, per-country
                                line-of-best-fit scatter, and multi-country grid (Figures 3, 5).
  plots_beta_lobf_grid.R       Grid-cell beta_i, for all 6 groups (full + 5 leave-one-model-
                                out variants): histogram, world raster map, and CONUS raster
                                map per group (Figures 1, 6 for "full"), sharing one fixed
                                color scale so groups are directly comparable.
  plots_stats_fpm_all.R        Descriptive plots and summary stats of fire PM2.5 across all
                                three studies, globally and for the USA.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
############################  4 - DATA INPUTS  #######################################
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

input/pierce_etal_2017/    CESM gridded PM2.5 NetCDFs (2000 baseline, 2050/2100 x RCP4.5/8.5,
                            each with all-PM, no-fire, and human-influence variants; 0.9x1.25deg,
                            monthly); CLM population-density NetCDFs (SSP1/SSP3, 0.5deg,
                            1850-2100); CESM GMT anomaly NetCDFs (RCP4.5/8.5).

input/Park_etal_2024/      GEOS-Chem surface PM2.5 output (.nc4) for 3 wildfire-vegetation
                            models (CLASSIC, JULES, SSiB4) x 6 decades (1960s-2010s), factual
                            and counterfactual, plus a withoutfire baseline; population grid
                            (pop_grid_6515.mat, 0.5deg x 6 decades).

input/Zhao_etal_2025/      Machine-learning-projected PM2.5 (0.1deg CSVs, SSP2-4.5/SSP5-8.5 x
                            with/without fire, ~2095-2099) and population (.npz, 0.1deg, 2010).

input/GIVE/                GIVE_countries.csv: the country list (ISO3) used by the GIVE IAM,
                            the reference set that beta_c is ultimately joined onto.

input/WB_crude_death_rate/ World Bank crude death rate per 1,000 people, by country and year
                            (1960-2020); used to fill baseline mortality for countries/cells
                            without a direct match.

input/landmask_area/       Grid-cell area (km^2) at 0.5deg, used to convert population density
                            to population totals.

input/temperature/         GMT anomaly series feeding temp_chg.R: Pierce CESM NetCDFs, OWID
                            observed annual anomaly (for Park decades), and MimiSSP SSP2-4.5 /
                            SSP5-8.5 series (for Zhao scenarios).

